course: dictionary
lesson: 6116
title: Words from machines and everyday life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A microphone is a device that picks up sound and turns it into an electrical signal, so the sound can be made louder, recorded or sent somewhere else. Mic and mike are short, informal ways of saying it.
explain: «When you ring Grandma, your phone's microphone turns the wobbles of your voice into electric signals.» The clue is the job it does: it takes sound and changes it into something a machine can use. Ask: what would fit here? Try microphone in place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: A speaker does the opposite. «A microphone turns sound wobbles into electric signals, and a speaker turns signals back into sound.» When two words are used side by side like this, the text is often showing you how they are different.
explain: You will also hear phrases such as speak into the microphone, the mic is on, and open mic. Each phrase follows the same idea: the microphone is the part that picks up your voice.
fact: A microphone changes sound into an electrical signal.
fact: A speaker changes an electrical signal back into sound.
fact: «Mic» and «mike» are informal short forms of microphone.
fact: «A microphone left on» means it is still picking up sound, so people can hear what is said near it.
fact: «Only in 1938 did special microphones prove bats use ultrasound», which shows that scientists used microphones to find out things about the natural world.
exercise: «A microphone left on can let everyone in the game hear what is happening in your home.» What does a microphone do? | It stops sound from travelling | *It picks up sound and turns it into an electrical signal | It turns electric signals into shaking air only | It makes pictures appear on a screen
exercise: Ravi says, «The mic is on.» What does he mean? | He is eating a snack | The microphone is broken and silent | *The microphone is switched on and picking up sound | He has turned off the speaker
exercise: «A microphone turns sound wobbles into electric signals, and a speaker turns signals back into sound.» What does a speaker do? | *It turns electrical signals back into sound | It records pictures | It picks up sound and makes it electric | It turns sound into numbers
test: «When you ring Grandma, your phone's microphone turns the wobbles of your voice into electric signals, and the phone turns those into numbers.» Which word is an informal short form of microphone? | Speaker | Wobble | Ring | *Mic
test: «Only in 1938 did special microphones prove bats use ultrasound.» What did the microphones prove? | *That bats use ultrasound | That bats can see with their ears | That bats never crash into threads | That bats cannot hear at all
exam: Which word best fits here? A microphone ___ sound into an electrical signal. | *turns | shouts | hides | sleeps
